{"type":"text","timestamp":1794254364358,"sessionID":"ses_e3e1fa429ffeKdBPR0VbYYeFeh","part":{"id":"prt_1c1e4dea9001mC1LKceU3n7duj","messageID":"msg_1c1e4c950001TP73CtBGuB73z0","sessionID":"ses_e3e1fa429ffeKdBPR0VbYYeFeh","type":"text","text":"The calendar is built: the Flask API, the SQLite storage under `./data` and the React frontend. I couldn't test the Docker image because Docker isn't available here.\n\nWhat I did run:\n- **Backend:** the register, login, create, update, list and delete endpoints behave as specified in a quick scripted check.\n- **Server:** it starts under gunicorn, `GET /api/health` returns `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`, and it serves the frontend page at `/`.\n- **Frontend:** `npm run build` passes, including the TypeScript check.\n- **Not run:** I haven't clicked through the frontend in a browser.\n\nBehaviours you might not assume:\n- **Auth:** login returns the `token` plus the `username`. Tokens expire after 30 days, and I added `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/auth/me`.\n- **Validation:** errors come back as 400 with `{\"error\": ..., \"errors\": {field: message}}`, and the forms show those messages. Passwords need at least 6 characters, usernames are case-insensitive, and a duplicate username gets 409. An end time before the start time is rejected.\n- **Date range:** `start_date` and `end_date` accept a date or a date-time. A bare `end_date` covers that whole day, and an event overlapping the range counts as inside it.\n- **Frontend:** it keeps the token in `localStorage`. Clicking a day cell opens the day view.\n\nI added a `.gitignore` for `node_modules`, `frontend/dist`, `__pycache__` and `data/`. I also added Tailwind (`tailwindcss` and `@tailwindcss/vite`) and TypeScript to the frontend dependencies, so `package.json` and `package-lock.json` changed.","time":{"start":1794254364329,"end":1794254364334}}}
